//
//  CaltrainCorridor.swift
//  caltrain-enhanced
//
//  The shape of the railway itself: one centreline from San Francisco to Gilroy, with a
//  vertex pinned at every platform, so a line drawn between two stops follows the track
//  instead of cutting across the map. Straight station-to-station hops read as obviously
//  wrong through Brisbane, San Bruno and Coyote valley, where the corridor bends for
//  miles at a time.
//
//  Auto-generated from OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL) — the
//  Caltrain Peninsula Subdivision, plus UP's Coast Subdivision south of Diridon, with
//  the parallel tracks collapsed to their median. Do not edit by hand.
//

